gano - a simple console text editor written in GNU Guile
========================================================

Running
-------

Requires Guile 3.0.  gano runs from the source tree (there is no
`make install` yet):

    bin/gano [FILE]
    bin/gano --help | --version

Run `make` first to byte-compile the modules; without it, the first run
compiles them into .cache/guile, which takes about 20 seconds.

Files are read and written as UTF-8, keeping their line endings and
whether they end with a newline.  A file that is not valid UTF-8 opens
with its bad bytes shown as U+FFFD, and gano asks before saving over it.

Keys
----

^G shows every command with its keys, and A-x runs any command by name
(Tab completes the name).  ^ means Ctrl; A- means Alt (or Esc, then the
key).  The main ones:

    arrows, Home/End, PgUp/PgDn   move (also ^A/^E, ^Y/^V)
    C-left/C-right, C-up/C-down   move by word / paragraph
    A-\ / A-/                     first / last line
    ^_ or A-g                     go to line[,column]
    Backspace, Delete             delete (joining lines at line ends)
    ^^ (Ctrl+6) or A-a            start selecting
    ^K / A-6 / ^U                 cut / copy / paste: the selection if
                                  there is one, else the line
                                  (consecutive cuts or copies are
                                  pasted together)
    A-u / A-e                     undo / redo
    ^W / A-q                      search forward / backward
    ^\ or A-r                     replace, asking at each match
                                  (Y/N, A for all the rest, ^C to stop)
    ^S                            save (asks for a name if there is none)
    ^O                            write out under a new name
    ^X                            exit (offers to save unsaved changes)
    ^Q                            exit, discarding unsaved changes
    ^C                            show the cursor position; at a prompt,
                                  cancel
    ^L                            redraw the screen (after line noise, say);
                                  works at prompts and in the help too

At the search, replace and go-to-line prompts, ^Y and ^V go to the
first and last line.  The keys are kept in a command table
(src/gano/commands.scm), which the help rows and ^G screen are made
from.

Building and testing
--------------------

A plain Makefile; Guile and guild are found with pkg-config (guile-3.0,
from the Guile development package; set GUILE_PC for another).

    make                         # byte-compile into build/, with warnings
    make check                   # run all the test suites
    make dist                    # gano-VERSION.tar.gz
    make distcheck               # build and check the tarball unpacked
    make clean

The suites can also be run directly:

    test/run-all.sh              # every suite, one summary line each
    test/run-all.sh editor       # just test/test-editor.scm

Layout
------

    Makefile                build, check, dist
    bin/gano                launcher script
    src/gano/editor.scm     the editor: state, key handling, screen
    src/gano/commands.scm   command registry: names, help, modes, shortcuts
    src/gano/buffer.scm     one import for the character buffer layers
    src/gano/cbuf-*.scm     the character buffer (core, basic, standard,
                            extra, serialization, utils)
    src/gano/frame.scm      viewport onto a buffer
    src/gano/screen.scm     screen contents, and the fewest bytes that turn
                            the screen the terminal shows into a new one
    src/gano/terminal.scm   raw mode, ANSI output, key input
    src/gano/keys.scm       key objects
    src/gano/text-metrics.scm, char.scm, wcwidth.scm, ...
                            Unicode text measurement (left to right)
    tools/                  the wcwidth table generator, compile cache helper
    attic/                  earlier experiments, kept for reference
